  partName: Left Center Bolt
  description: The Left Center Bolt is a tiny, complex-shaped fastener located at
    the top-left-front of the engine, made of Material.001, serving as a critical
    component in the engine's mounting system. Its high-strength material and precise
    threading enable it to secure the engine's center section, maintaining stability
    and balance. Interestingly, the Left Center Bolt's complex shape allows for a
    snug fit, preventing damage from vibration and movement.
